rs.githubusercontent.com/u/138339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm","html_url":"https://github.com/arsenm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"73a0b12b8ee34b9d2858cf6ca60a6154145a52ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/73a0b12b8ee34b9d2858cf6ca60a6154145a52ca","html_url":"https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commit/73a0b12b8ee34b9d2858cf6ca60a6154145a52ca"}]},{"sha":"7c9ae52cfdce9b7fc6f06b1a5f3a54f9a2f2d0ec","node_id":"C_kwDOE3b639oAKDdjOWFlNTJjZmRjZTliN2ZjNmYwNmIxYTVmM2E1NGY5YTJmMmQwZWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Matt Arsenault","email":"Matthew.Arsenault@amd.com","date":"2026-09-30T07:42:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-30T07:42:10Z"},"message":"TwoAddressInstructions: Use the per-operand early clobber flag for tied copies (#227581)\n\nThe live interval update for the copy inserted for a tied operand ended\nthe new segment at getRegSlot(IsEarlyClobber), using a flag computed\nonce per instruction for any tied pairs. Use the flag\nof the def actually being processed.\n\nWith an inline asm mixing \"=&r\" and \"=r\" outputs tied to the same input,\nthe copy for the plain def ended at the early clobber slot, leaving a\nhole before its own def. That splits the live range into multiple\nconnected components and asserts in updatePressureDiffs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c78796b60f11b8b24e86b4ac373a271824a903d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/git/trees/6c78796b60f11b8b24e86b4ac373a271824a903d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/git/commits/7c9ae52cfdce9b7fc6f06b1a5f3a54f9a2f2d0ec","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvL1SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX/YQADUFpYjZhr/QFU5IyRzpcoSU\nKsoEZJKvK1wbT7ghhz+2PLsLv8e9wj6BzrgwErXwLS5QoBhMLW1kY80FXpfZ5cNS\nlTv+ktp38DLE+wctwQHIs8HAOWhZjAy9+M13/7PWN4ant2xOSKER0LV2J2bNEucT\n2ahc+52cSpjUiyoOCqvf8nmXnOGz+33HR+13zJRL5vFVxbtq+dTTAj9uEL2Qm+ty\nJspylGqWXqr5VF2yx4hDxQVpoaiHEqdR63PSO5OqVhOzfjzJYxrk04N2wR+o7TnA\nYTm55MWVuoitwcj9qw5Ix6PYyTpz08SRmOCbNwNYSkBfBMNSLSETbwd5gtkIIU7k\n8Zw0wnSwy1EXo+QiWVS3lK66Sm1kxNIJhml+JxUkhKLzJY6CXkX8txztjI0B6nF4\nyh7pmS1WukXNszYIMEJIRVBp01TOsaijATj6Av6PMId4wil3Nq5skwWrpjdStqhY\ng2RgmUuBo2YKQTyMzCQbFww90do7f1YxT++MtcyPZCo+dW9PLhHKkfbOWacBCb4O\nSn7Pm4g7h2HfEUiunVQntocA2zbOnF2CMePq41JRqk7JvIt7CeJT25IWRiMZGR6J\nbo28KfS0LYXNAsxNn9dG2zr+JdihT75ENV1pqZ07K0edh5dLKKVlnU/QfYeYoJn4\nTwaRlTbDmz8L8a0iaUdD\n=E5wx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6c78796b60f11b8b24e86b4ac373a271824a903d\nparent 7778bb2082b8e64528b691f1b7a7016e8bd64860\nauthor Matt Arsenault <Matthew.Arsenault@amd.com> 1790754130 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790754130 +0200\n\nTwoAddressInstructions: Use the per-operand early clobber flag for tied copies (#227581)\n\nThe live interval update for the copy inserted for a tied operand ended\nthe new segment at getRegSlot(IsEarlyClobber), using a flag computed\nonce per instruction for any tied pairs. Use the flag\nof the def actually being processed.\n\nWith an inline asm mixing \"=&r\" and \"=r\" outputs tied to the same input,\nthe copy for the plain def ended at the early clobber slot, leaving a\nhole before its own def. That splits the live range into multiple\nconnected components and asserts in updatePressureDiffs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-05T01:12:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/7c9ae52cfdce9b7fc6f06b1a5f3a54f9a2f2d0ec","html_url":"https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commit/7c9ae52cfdce9b7fc6f06b1a5f3a54f9a2f2d0ec","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/7c9ae52cfdce9b7fc6f06b1a5f3a54f9a2f2d0ec/comments","author":{"login":"arsenm","id":138339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODMzOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm","html_url":"https://github.com/arsenm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7778bb2082b8e64528b691f1b7a7016e8bd64860","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/7778bb2082b8e64528b691f1b7a7016e8bd64860","html_url":"https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commit/7778bb2082b8e64528b691f1b7a7016e8bd64860"}]},{"sha":"18ef19fb83d9d3fa369481bb0537be4fdf5552fb","node_id":"C_kwDOE3b639oAKDE4ZWYxOWZiODNkOWQzZmEzNjk0ODFiYjA1MzdiZTRmZGY1NTUyZmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Vitaly Buka","email":"vitalybuka@google.com","date":"2026-09-30T07:10:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-30T07:10:10Z"},"message":"[TwoAddressInstruction] Drop physreg ranges after unfolding a load (#227538)\n\nSince #225174 LiveIntervals is computed before TwoAddressInstructions.\nWhen tryInstructionTransform() unfolds a load, e.g. OR64rm into\nMOV64rm + OR64rr, it calls repairIntervalsInRange(). That function\nonly repairs virtual registers. If the regunit range of a physreg def\nof the original instruction ($eflags here) was already cached, it\nkeeps a value defined at the slot of the erased instruction.\n\nThe machine verifier then reports \"No instruction at VNInfo def index\"\nand later passes hit `LR.verify()` in LiveIntervals::HMEditor. This\nbroke the MSan bootstrap build of clang/lib/Sema/SemaAPINotes.cpp.\n\nDrop the cached regunit ranges for the physregs of the unfolded\ninstruction so they are recomputed on demand. MachineBasicBlock.cpp\nalready does the same after repairIntervalsInRange().\n\nAssisted-by: Gemini","tree":{"sha":"c13738c662b47a177dd341c7d01187a07b6495b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/git/trees/c13738c662b47a177dd341c7d01187a07b6495b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/git/commits/18ef19fb83d9d3fa369481bb0537be4fdf5552fb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvLXSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoU0QAK0QAjQyAUrP3qaYhv2WnQYL\npdmoXi6UD9Q4VPUb9JXsqM0mVSy4wrm5e73edm9pb2ZnhbkQ3rAQU3MD8YQCXacd\nps7zRDCmSVtMCDxBdQkbeDxClXemo3htqCoi0bU6g9zgCBEMuQ3FAMvjJ1PVRnFO\nGo1jqCs9Frjkm5jtO8Gd+B9HhMXrghGp1w5Jmuc185U8gQhIWla9ssK/8l2n3lzx\noC9JSYs9ebcbFFEnrSSZ6o3VjV5ID5wO78Gy7tPBn3KBaxkcGWdX5baYZRkoOw0+\nlHaBT4wACX2D+ugNspDzfyEmkGjMIAc8nmrzC5NA68PXuojZfjl44aBUunmccic/\nssUJL7E3zua/AnOxkb8h1Bta89BPwk/uu1xjyeyXD5JzMj8WT2Wq83fRgn/zx7dz\n9sQOwEJbDNPkyQU75eplXTqR/CV1s3kXPpNqL/dcBcIbiPshmguP/GUttsoXb7zR\nDgRbAImt7SCQChvExqCDRloyFWvDG5v303KWWoKJlz7wiejJuLqbNy6dloYR7XzQ\nIy/EbVnCjGSJMciDKIWxm29Ve74K/7g82Tf8DQCgengvxnEbEB1XjG04nDg6csHA\nRD/temJfI7fpIkAsZs7l/den+7+yspDTrMk+2tAHAjVpoye7k8FGrrR+UEU3MI4i\nx7B3TMGvXZ/iz9X74SEy\n=fL3f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c13738c662b47a177dd341c7d01187a07b6495b1\nparent 65e323a85f0d2e63a5f6c97e8ce2bd8e989aacf4\nauthor Vitaly Buka <vitalybuka@google.com> 1790752210 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790752210 -0700\n\n[TwoAddressInstruction] Drop physreg ranges after unfolding a load (#227538)\n\nSince #225174 LiveIntervals is computed before TwoAddressInstructions.\nWhen tryInstructionTransform() unfolds a load, e.g. OR64rm into\nMOV64rm + OR64rr, it calls repairIntervalsInRange(). That function\nonly repairs virtual registers. If the regunit range of a physreg def\nof the original instruction ($eflags here) was already cached, it\nkeeps a value defined at the slot of the erased instruction.\n\nThe machine verifier then reports \"No instruction at VNInfo def index\"\nand later passes hit `LR.verify()` in LiveIntervals::HMEditor. This\nbroke the MSan bootstrap build of clang/lib/Sema/SemaAPINotes.cpp.\n\nDrop the cached regunit ranges for the physregs of the unfolded\ninstruction so they are recomputed on demand. MachineBasicBlock.cpp\nalready does the same after repairIntervalsInRange().\n\nAssisted-by: Gemini","verified_at":"2026-10-05T01:12:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/18ef19fb83d9d3fa369481bb0537be4fdf5552fb","html_url":"https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commit/18ef19fb83d9d3fa369481bb0537be4fdf5552fb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/18ef19fb83d9d3fa369481bb0537be4fdf5552fb/comments","author":{"login":"vitalybuka","id":1531415,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzE0MTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1531415?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka","html_url":"https://github.com/vitalybuka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitalybuka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"65e323a85f0d2e63a5f6c97e8ce2bd8e989aacf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/65e323a85f0d2e63a5f6c97e8ce2bd8e989aacf4","html_url":"https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commit/65e323a85f0d2e63a5f6c97e8ce2bd8e989aacf4"}]},{"sha":"a3db7fe43c223144d4667a78444cc01901e5b9da","node_id":"C_kwDOE3b639oAKGEzZGI3ZmU0M2MyMjMxNDRkNDY2N2E3ODQ0NGNjMDE5MDFlNWI5ZGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Matt Arsenault","email":"Matthew.Arsenault@amd.com","date":"2026-09-29T21:32:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-29T21:32:22Z"},"message":"TwoAddressInstructions: Fix subranges straddling the INSERT_SUBREG subreg index (#227427)\n\nRewriting INSERT_SUBREG into a subregister COPY narrows the def from the\nwhole register down to one subreg index. The live interval fixup for that only \nhandled subranges entirely disjoint from the inserted lane mask, so a partially \noverlapping subrange keeps a value whose def no longer writes all of its lanes.\n    \nThe stale value makes the lanes outside the inserted subregister look\ndefined by the COPY, so the copy that actually provides them ends up\ndead and its value is lost. Refine the subranges against the subreg index\nbefore narrowing the def, leaving each one either fully redefined by the COPY\nor untouched by it.\n    \nFixes a miscompile reported on RISC-V and restores the pre-6286f77214be\noutput of Thumb2/mve-vst2.ll, Thumb2/mve-vst3.ll and PowerPC/dmr-enable.ll.\n    \nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a7dee5458261256d938e6991490dc31d12a9d073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/git/trees/a7dee5458261256d938e6991490dc31d12a9d073"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/git/commits/a3db7fe43c223144d4667a78444cc01901e5b9da","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvC5nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4t4QAGfWJ9x2FgwqLEb20XgyCJV6\nGFBCdxWs9pSo35PqJ+sOeIH5VcJ4no101JEju8GF1AEZzHiLKtinhltIFJ8wurJb\nV24X/C+CrSF66R8431UX5AM/g8zGq0oKspFrUYWIcb+582oY4M2aHHCjw9nJuzwl\nNxutET8DzFc1lmb7gSmbmsJdTTwDPWXTm6Bvvxat22pBpih/NSfbvznrT0Ok48hp\nuXo2ofbrd86KVcGF1+03kSYR3oIp07WgC0r7qd3+ANbXu3hRM/otYujzP5QtbE1+\nCnzrrb4Sqsy633erAvkqZxrMNinXsnFCKXeVxDBsNCre+X/PF8ALwhdOxcYocc3W\n9ZJQNzvjUXQ3BXUHQEHpjnPXp2yQ/W/shDL98BvthylHldhVJy8WRuATzOuJ5Xub\nMXLNCdv2VOYRrX3OtFB8+q2WBA8WmDaOfuY7hvL+2iOR8BeQecbnHa5sdopvrkNf\ngShda7++67Uo7S8wEApHezEXQzzPAENUYjkV8YDeDJJczfOSqVUZCJM1glGl2bJn\ntvE+jZKaJIUGx/e7taI7lVL70zcqveCVYkO6ewxj2V7GGnIZK2x4tI+r53C4kqb/\nMys08hVnm/+Kyu6ypI3F6rcfL9qlLr2X1Um3Z8pAUGbreOfgXfhVFWNY5CWI+kMj\nnzqaHSi1Roc6Jn2ujMgj\n=UXgp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a7dee5458261256d938e6991490dc31d12a9d073\nparent 56ee698b48ab31be816dbdfd4bea8c3761663dbe\nauthor Matt Arsenault <Matthew.Arsenault@amd.com> 1790717542 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790717542 +0000\n\nTwoAddressInstructions: Fix subranges straddling the INSERT_SUBREG subreg index (#227427)\n\nRewriting INSERT_SUBREG into a subregister COPY narrows the def from the\nwhole register down to one subreg index. The live interval fixup for that only \nhandled subranges entirely disjoint from the inserted lane mask, so a partially \noverlapping subrange keeps a value whose def no longer writes all of its lanes.\n    \nThe stale value makes the lanes outside the inserted subregister look\ndefined by the COPY, so the copy that actually provides them ends up\ndead and its value is lost. Refine the subranges against the subreg index\nbefore narrowing the def, leaving each one either fully redefined by the COPY\nor untouched by it.\n    \nFixes a miscompile reported on RISC-V and restores the pre-6286f77214be\noutput of Thumb2/mve-vst2.ll, Thumb2/mve-vst3.ll and PowerPC/dmr-enable.ll.\n    \nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-05T01:12:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/a3db7fe43c223144d4667a78444cc01901e5b9da","html_url":"https://github.com/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commit/a3db7fe43c223144d4667a78444cc01901e5b9da","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/llvm-mos/llvm-mos/commits/a3db7fe43c223144d4667a78444cc01901e5b9da/comments","author":{"login":"arsenm","id":138339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODMzOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm","html_url":"https://github.com/arsenm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arsenm/followers","fol